+### Metrics
+
+`mcpgw_registry_webhook_send_total{event_type, outcome}` counts every outbound send attempt. `outcome` is `sent` or `failed`. Because delivery is at-most-once (no retries), a consumer outage shows up as sustained `outcome="failed"` - alert on it:
+
+```promql
+rate(mcpgw_registry_webhook_send_total{outcome="failed"}[5m]) > 0
+```
+
+## Consumer Contract
+
+Consumers of these webhooks MUST NOT assume more than the registry guarantees:
+
+| Guarantee | Contract |
+|-----------|----------|
+| Ordering | NOT guaranteed. Events are sent from independent background tasks; a `scan_complete` may arrive after a later `update` for the same asset. Never infer state from receipt order. |
+| Delivery | At-most-once. No retries, no dead-letter queue. A failed delivery is logged and counted in the `failed` metric, then dropped. |
+| Idempotency | Deduplicate on `event_id` (UUID per delivery attempt). Key your dedupe window on `event_id` alone - not on `(asset, event_type)` pairs. |
+| Unknown events | Skip unknown `event_type` values without failing. New event types may be added. |
+| Integrity | When `REGISTRATION_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET` is configured, verify `X-Registry-Signature` per the rules above before trusting an event. An unsigned deployment trusts whoever can reach the receiver URL. |
+
 In ECS deployments, these log messages appear in the registry task's CloudWatch Log Group.
 
